## Slide 10

Task Form Groups

Task Form Groups
An organizational only level of grouping to help manage large numbers of Task Forms
Task Forms
A collection of Task Form that can be assigned to a Task Definition.  They can be assigned to multiple Task Definitions

## Slide 11

Task Form Groups

Task Form Groups
An organizational only level of grouping to help manage large numbers of Task Forms
Task Forms
A collection of Task Form that can be assigned to a Task Definition.  They can be assigned to multiple Task Definitions

## Slide 12

Task Form Item Groups

Task Form Item Groups
An organizational only level of grouping within a Task Form
Task Form Items
The individual inputs within a Task that are collected. They contain various properties that determine how they render and how they are validated

## Slide 13

Task Form Item Groups

Task Form Item Groups
An organizational only level of grouping within a Task Form.

Task Form Items
The individual inputs within a Task that are collected. They contain various properties that determine how they render and how they are validated.

## Slide 14

Task Form Item Properties 

Data Type
Drives the displayed form input type and validation in standard Pages and Parts.
Render Type
Overrides the standard rendering based on Data Type.
Prompt
An alternate label displayed on standard Pages and Parts.
Default Value
The value of the item when the Task is created and before it is edited by a User.
Minimum/Maximum
Used for automatic validation in standard Pages and Parts.
Require Change
If checked, a User must change the item’s value to something different than the Default Value.

